168		// Optional! Only one of {A2Go1, A2Go2, A2Go3} is required!
169	
170		// Compute the mean edge length. This will be the "target length".
171	
172	    // Repeat the four main steps for `outer_iterations` iterations:
173	
174	    // -> Split edges much longer than the target length.
175		//     ("much longer" means > target length * params.longer_factor)
176	
177	    // -> Collapse edges much shorter than the target length.
178		//     ("much shorter" means < target length * params.shorter_factor)
179	
180	    // -> Flip each edge if it improves vertex degree.
181	
182	    // -> Finally, apply some tangential smoothing to the vertex positions.
183		//     This means move every vertex in the plane of its normal,
184		//     toward the centroid of its neighbors, by params.smoothing_step of
185		//     the total distance (so, smoothing_step of 1 would move all the way,
186		//     smoothing_step of 0 would not move).
187		// -> Repeat the tangential smoothing part params.smoothing_iterations times.
188	
189		//NOTE: many of the steps in this function will be modifying the element
190		//      lists they are looping over. Take care to avoid use-after-free
191		//      or infinite-loop problems.
192	
193	}
